{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779115-2ed-primeval-miasma","id":779115,"title":"[2ed] Primeval Miasma","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-03T11:25:25-08:00","id":779115,"title":"[2ed] Primeval Miasma","content":"Hi all,<br /> <br /> I have a question about using Primeval Miasma to hurt a Vampire.<br /> It says:<br /> <br /> &quot;\u200bthe vampire can instead force herself into the victim\u2019s lungs with<br /> strands of semi-tangible smoke, stealing her life-force along<br /> with her breath (grapple and \u201cbite\u201d using her normal Physical<br /> Attributes).&quot;<br /> <br /> Does it works even on undead? Should the PC make a grapple maneuver to get inside the Lungs and then *bite* normally stealing the vitae and dealing a lethal damage for each vitae taken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 12-03-2015, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:10:05-08:00","id":779154,"title":"","content":"Well, vampires don't breath, so probably breath-drinking shouldn't work against them, only against living beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T14:51:34-08:00","id":779291,"title":"","content":"It's a judgment call for the ST, but I think it wouldn't work. Even Strix can't &quot;Breath Drink&quot; a Revenant or Kindred. If it did work though then it'd use the normal violent feeding rules.<br /> <br /> Turn 1 - Roll to grapple (resisted by the targets defense)<br /> Turn 2 - Roll to &quot;bite&quot; to enter the lungs (contested by the victims grapple check). Extra successes deal more damage, but only <u>one</u> Vitae is drained.<br /> Turn 3+ - Roll to &quot;feed&quot;. (contested by the victim's grapple check) Extra successes mean more Vitae drained per turn, capped by Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> (All of this assumes normal successes on the attackers part and no frenzy)<br /> <br /> In any case, only mortals take lethal damage per point of Vitae drained. Vitae losses come directly out of a kindred's or revenant's Vitae pool. Well, until they run out and amaranth begins. At which point they take damage, but the attacker doesn't get Vitae for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 12-03-2015, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T15:37:16-08:00","id":779329,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I think I'll not let this work on a vampire. I wanted just have more opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T15:49:31-08:00","id":780184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779115-2ed-primeval-miasma#post779115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;\u200b stealing her life-force along<br /> with her breath</div> </div> </div> </div>I would take that bit as the Key wording. They go in there to steal the life-force. Vampires have it. it's the vitae that wakes them that keeps them moving. The breath is just an additional. &quot;along with her breath&quot; comes as a secondary effect from stealing the life. I think it just wouldnt make the vampire gasp and choke for air. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T21:52:18-08:00","id":780384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779115-2ed-primeval-miasma?p=780184#post780184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would take that bit as the Key wording. They go in there to steal the life-force. Vampires have it. it's the vitae that wakes them that keeps them moving. The breath is just an additional. &quot;along with her breath&quot; comes as a secondary effect from stealing the life. I think it just wouldnt make the vampire gasp and choke for air. </div> </div> </div> </div>That would also be consistent with the fact that feeding on a vampire doesn't cause them damage (apart from damage taken from the Bite), only Vitae loss. It's not the interpretation I would use, but it's a perfectly reasonable one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T21:59:01-08:00","id":780387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779115-2ed-primeval-miasma?p=780384#post780384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would also be consistent with the fact that feeding on a vampire doesn't cause them damage (apart from damage taken from the Bite), only Vitae loss. It's not the interpretation I would use, but it's a perfectly reasonable one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From the rules for diablerie on p101, 'Once a Kindred victim is completely without Vitae, each point that would otherwise be taken becomes instead one point of lethal damage.' Diablerie doesn't kick in until you fill their boxes with Aggravated damage, at which point you either start the diablerie or just send them to their Final Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T22:13:27-08:00","id":780391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779115-2ed-primeval-miasma?p=780387#post780387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the rules for diablerie on p101, 'Once a Kindred victim is completely without Vitae, each point that would otherwise be taken becomes instead one point of lethal damage.' Diablerie doesn't kick in until you fill their boxes with Aggravated damage, at which point you either start the diablerie or just send them to their Final Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but they don't start taking the damage until they're out of Vitae, and at that point the feeding vampire isn't gaining Vitae out of it, so I imagine the damage is something more supernatural in nature than blood loss or suffocation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T22:38:01-08:00","id":780404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779115-2ed-primeval-miasma?p=780391#post780391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but they don't start taking the damage until they're out of Vitae, and at that point the feeding vampire isn't gaining Vitae out of it, so I imagine the damage is something more supernatural in nature than blood loss or suffocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I certainly wouldn't allow the use of something like Physical Intensity in that state to drain off Vitae.<br /> <br /> The situation reminds me of the Brothers of Ypres, one of my favorite bloodlines. Borne as a victim of chemical warfare, they can poison people and turn into a cloud of poison. Because vampires were immune to this they ended up with a Discipline that was effectively useless against other vampires, giving them a disadvantage in internecine conflict they tried to conceal.<br /> <br /> Of course, Protean has many other uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T01:09:18-08:00","id":780445,"title":"","content":"It's a judgment call, but I still lean towards it not working on vampires. Strix can't breath drink a Kindred because, &quot;their Vitae is bound inexorably to their blood&quot; The same logic should apply to Primeval Miasma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T02:55:54-08:00","id":780466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jaerys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/779115-2ed-primeval-miasma?p=780445#post780445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a judgment call, but I still lean towards it not working on vampires. Strix can't breath drink a Kindred because, &amp;quot;their Vitae is bound inexorably to their blood&amp;quot; The same logic should apply to Primeval Miasma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I agree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T10:00:51-08:00","id":780598,"title":"","content":"I am almost positive it says somewhere vampires with Blush of Life can bleed... but the vitae hides somewhere or wells up at the wound, but does not exit. so the blood drips, but the vitae stays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T11:28:30-08:00","id":780636,"title":"","content":"Yes I read it too. Nevertheless kindred steal vitae from other kindred drinking their blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}